{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484832-spirit-questing-mage","id":1484832,"title":"Spirit questing mage.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-23T18:31:28-07:00","id":1484832,"title":"Spirit questing mage.","content":"It has been a long while, but I believe if you go into the Umbra with some sort of quest in mind, some boon you wish to bring back to the material world, the Umbra will subtly guide your journey to help you find what you seek. Can someone give me some story ideas on how to guide a Mage seeking a Djinn willing to be a familiar and who wont simply kill him on sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T07:09:26-07:00","id":1484865,"title":"","content":"Well, on one hand, Djinn are duplicitous. So, it could involve some &quot;helpful&quot; Djinn (perhaps masquerading as another spirit) saying that's going to guide the mage/s, but only to lure them into a trap. Classic 1001 nigths shenanigan. Doesn't need to be one that has to be solved by force, could be a test of wits too.<br /> <br /> Also, a lesson. Djinn typically *aren't* willing to be a familiar. Taftani force the deal, and never go to the Umbra.<br /> <br /> But, if perseverant, this could lead to a travel to the City of Brass. A place where mages aren't welcome, but like the jinn they may be able to masquerade as a spirit or Djinn (maybe the duplicitous Djinn used an artifact of sorts, or accepted to provide cover after beaten)<br /> <br /> Maybe there the mage could find a Djinn that has been ostracized by the others for some reason. Maybe broke a taboo or had bad luck - invent some reason of why these proud beings of smokless fire would treat some of their own with what even them would perceive as &quot;injustice&quot;. Perhaps such a being could accept to be in a relationship with a mage that treats with respect, and not as a Paradox container.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}